  "worked_solution": "For the die, there is a total of $6$ outcomes: $1,2,3,4,5,6.$\n\nFor the coin, there are just $2$ outcomes: \"Heads\" and \"Tails\".\n\nUsing the **rule of product**, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Total Possible Outcomes} & =\\text{Number of outcomes on the\u00a0}1\\text{st roll of the die} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of outcomes on the\u00a0}2\\text{nd roll of the die} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of outcomes on the\u00a0}1\\text{st flip of the coin} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of outcomes on the\u00a0}2\\text{nd flip of the coin} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of outcomes on the\u00a0}3\\text{rd flip of the coin} \\\\  & =6\\times 6\\times 2\\times 2\\times 2 \\\\  & ={6}^{2}\\times {2}^{3} \\\\  & =36\\times 8 \\\\  & =288.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, there are $288$ possible outcomes.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
